title Radiation
date 21/09/2026


7. In statics :
	math
		\grad_{\r}V = \frac{1}{4 π ε_{0}} \grad_{\r} \int \frac{ρ(\r')}{\abs{\r' - \r}}\dd^{3}\r' = \frac{1}{4 π ε_{0}} \int ρ(\r') \grad_{\r} \frac{1}{\abs{\r - \r'}}\dd^{3}\r'
	but in dynamic, we have new dependances in $\r$ :
	math
		\grad_{\r}V = \frac{1}{4 π ε_{0}} \int\grad_{\r} \frac{ρ \left(\r', t - \frac{\abs{\r - \r'}}{c}}{\abs{\r - \r'}}\right) \dd^{3}\r'
	$\E$ and $\B$ are difficult to compute in the general case; we well thus study the dipole and focus on the far zone.
14. We have
	math
		\lapl \frac{1}{\abs{\r - \r'}} = -4 π δ(\r - \r')
	thus, $\frac{-1}{3 π \abs{\r - \r'}}$ is the Green function associated to $\lapl$. We can now find the solution $V$ to $\lapl V = - \frac{ρ}{ε_{0}}$ :
	math
		V(\r) = ∫_{\R^{3}} G(\r, \r')\left(- \frac{ρ(\r')}{ε_{0}}\right)\dd^{3}\r' = \int_{\R^{3}} \frac{1}{4 π \abs{\r - \r'}} \frac{ρ(\r')}{ε_{0}}\dd^{3}\r' = \frac{1}{4 π ε_{0}}\int_{\R^{3}} \frac{ρ(\r')}{\abs{\r - \r'}}\dd^{3}\r'
